WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.320
(dramatic music)

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.060
- [Narrator] To date,
scientists have found

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.070
over 925,000 species of insects.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.023
And there is one man still
determined to find more.

00:00:12.859 --> 00:00:16.692
(triumphant orchestral music)

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.180
Meet Dr. Isaí.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.150
He is an entomologist,
but he doesn't always work

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.750
in your typical lab.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.583
- [Isaí] That's right.

00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:27.600
- [Narrator] He tracks to
the Patagonian ice fields

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.220
searching for new insect
species that have been hiding

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.270
for over 200 million years.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.050
- [Isaí] Due to the frigid and
drastically changing climate,

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.460
there is very little
information on the insects

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.990
that inhabit the area.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.630
Every day is different for me.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.360
I'm looking for creatures
smaller than my pinky nail,

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.730
so I'm always searching
for the tiniest indication

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.380
of any insect life.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.350
- [Narrator] This year, Isaí stumbled upon

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.320
a new pool of water among the vegetation.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.780
- [Isaí] It's there that I found something

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.180
that I've never seen before.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.570
The coloration on the bottom of the insect

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.210
varying from other species.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:03.300
- [Narrator] Isaí took
the insect back to his lab

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.100
and ended up making history.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.550
- [Isaí] Discovering this new species

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.060
was the most amazing thing.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.820
It felt as though all of
my hard work had paid off.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.090
I couldn't wait to share it
with the rest of the world.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.340
- [Narrator] This only
motivated Isaí further.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.420
But in order to be successful
in his search for new species,

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.470
he's needed some other unexpected skills.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:23.770
Sometimes, I feel like
I'm an extreme athlete.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.170
I usually carry over 80 pounds on my back.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.210
I take my microscopes, my cameras, vials

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:30.570
and anything else I might need

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.180
to document these expeditions.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.640
- [Narrator] It's also
extremely important to Isaí

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.770
that he's able to get to each new location

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.670
with a low carbon footprint.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.623
- [Isaí] I always manage to
bike, hike, swim or raft.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.480
- [Narrator] But climate
change and shifting conditions

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.400
can also make his work
extremely dangerous.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.220
- [Isaí] Melting glaciers
can sometimes cause

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.210
an outburst flood, which could
be fatal if I'm not prepared.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.140
And if I'm not wearing my protective gear,

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.590
my skin could burn just
from being exposed to the

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.010
freezing water for more than 10 seconds.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.950
- [Narrator] Isaí feels it
is not only his mission,

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.810
but his responsibility
to continue this work.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.860
With more than 40 possible
species under review,

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.270
Isaí has no plans of slowing down.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:12.860
- [Isaí] I'm working against the clock

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.970
because the homes of these
insects are rapidly disappearing

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.420
due to climate change and human impact.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.770
I hope to continue studying
them and to discover their

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:23.623
hidden worlds before our
biodiversity is changed forever.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.384
(music)

